+**The lead's note for this run (beta round 3, 2026-10-16).** You run in your own git worktree. First run `git fetch origin claude/stoic-ride-54ddxp && git checkout --detach origin/claude/stoic-ride-54ddxp`. Symlink today's crawl into it: `ln -s /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/wt-data2/data/snapshots data/snapshots; mkdir -p data/beta; ln -s /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/wt-data2/data/beta/snapshots data/beta/snapshots` (never commit them). The data is the 2026-10-16 crawl with every board whole, no cap: Amazon 22,179 postings, Apple 4,851, Google 3,821, NVIDIA 2,711, Microsoft 2,435, Meta 1,208, Netflix 414; main site Anduril 2,537. The lead's reviewer build is /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/cycle-beta6-dist; serve it and don't rebuild it. What changed since the last review: one-line notes with a Details disclosure (fix-density), Google grouped by job family with a Company filter (google-grouping), the salary audit fixes ("· 2 levels", per-place pay, no cut rows), first-page preview and a faster first render (perf-mobile-beta-2), and fix6-fresh-data. Read those sections of docs/process/lead.md first. Resume safety (the user, 2026-10-16: "if we get stop again due to limits, we're able to resume without losing much progress"): commit your files small and often in your worktree with explicit paths, keep a `## State` section at the top of your log, and send the lead your findings as you confirm them by SendMessage to "main". The lead checkpoints your worktree every 15 minutes; never push. Where the template says "don't commit", commit in your worktree anyway; the lead integrates. Give every server, browser or test command a timeout, so nothing can hang for hours. Other agents may run at the same time on a 4-CPU machine: note `uptime` with any timing. Check especially what changed since round 2: Amazon's whole board (22,179 postings) and Meta; the first-page preview on Amazon (real cards under "Loading 22,179 roles…", then the list replaces them); Google's job-family departments with the Company group-by and filter; the one-line notes with one Details disclosure (fix-density); "· 2 levels" and "· N places" cards, "from €X" minimums and shift-pay labels; the clusters chart, whose circles now sit at their postings' median pay, and the Ranges view, where identical posted bands are stacked into one row with ×N (viz-even). Also re-check that earlier findings stay fixed. Known open items you need not re-report, but may add evidence to: MR-23 (FX rates from 2026-07-01, waiting on the user), MR-26, MR-28, MR-29 (the on-screen label), MR-33 to MR-35, MR-37 to MR-42 in docs/process/methodology-review-beta-2.md, and the Insights tab on Amazon being one 4.3 s task (docs/process/perf-mobile-beta-2.md). You work in your own worktree, so do NOT edit docs/QA.md (another QA agent writes the same file at the same time): put your whole QA section, in docs/QA.md's format, at the end of your own log docs/process/qa-desktop-beta-3.md under a heading "## Section for docs/QA.md", and the lead copies it in when integrating.
+
+You are the desktop QA engineer for melon-seek (/home/user/melon-seek), "the Zillow of job postings". It is a zero-build vanilla-JS app that runs as a static site on GitHub Pages; there is also a server mode. Read README.md, docs/CONTRACT.md, docs/QA.md (especially the newest sections of docs/process/lead.md (from "Beta round 3" on: fix wave 5, fix-density, google-grouping, the salary audit, perf-mobile-beta-2, fix6-fresh-data), docs/process/methodology-review-beta.md, docs/process/ux-review-beta.md, docs/process/viz-review-beta.md and the 2026-10-11 beta sections of docs/QA.md), docs/process/PLAYBOOK.md and docs/process/TEMPLATE.md first.
+
+**Your job:** a thorough functional QA pass of the DESKTOP site for target `beta` (`/melon-seek/beta/` in a local build). Do not edit product code. You own:
+- a "Full QA pass (desktop, beta) 2026-10-16" section, appended to docs/QA.md;
+- docs/process/qa-desktop-beta-3.md, your process log;
+- docs/process/prompts/qa-desktop-beta-3.md (paste this prompt verbatim);
+- a NEW test file, test/e2e/beta-desktop-qa-3.e2e.js, registered the way scripts/e2e.js registers the others. Each bug you can reproduce gets a test that fails now and will pass once it is fixed. Give each test the bug ID in its name, e.g. `[D-3]`.
+Other QA agents append to docs/QA.md at the same time. Write only your own section, and re-read the file just before writing. Don't commit and never push.
+
+**Setup:**
+- The lead has already put the latest data in `data/beta/snapshots/` (scripts/cycle/local-data.js).
+- Build into your own folder, `node scripts/build-static.js --out /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/qa-desktop-beta-3/dist`, then `node scripts/cycle/serve.mjs --dist /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/qa-desktop-beta-3/dist --pid /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/qa-desktop-beta-3/serve.pid`; it prints the port. Never write the shared dist/: the lead built it for the e2e suite, and other agents run at the same time. Server mode: `PORT=<free port> node server/index.js`, with its own pid file.
+- Playwright: NODE_PATH=/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/pw/node_modules. Chromium is /opt/pw-browsers/chromium-1194/chrome-linux/chrome. Never run `playwright install`.
+- Viewports: 1440x900, 1280x800 and 1024x768, in light and dark.
+- Start every server with a pid file and stop it at the end. Never `pkill -f` or `pgrep -f`.
+
+**Test EVERY feature against real data, on all seven big-tech boards (Amazon, Apple, Google, Meta, Microsoft, NVIDIA and Netflix), plus Anduril from the main site for comparison:**
+- **Company and boards:** company menu search and switch, recent pills, "Add board" with a custom board.
+- **Search:** title matches rank first.
+- **Filters:**
+  - Salary: the slider, min/max inputs and "only with salary".
+  - Department, Location (canonical names), Seniority, Remote.
+  - The Responsibilities, Fit and Skills chips.
+  - "More": employment type, Listed, Juice grades.
+  - Clear all, and faceted counts staying consistent.
+- **Sorting:** every sort option.
+- **Chart:**
+  - Clusters, Ranges and Group by.
+  - A cluster click gives a chip, and dismissing it clears it.
+  - Hover and keyboard navigation, and the overflow markers.
+- **Map:** pins and tooltips, area chips, Pay|Juice and its legend, Remote, zoom, and resizing with the drawer open.
+- **Insights:** Compstimate (prefill, "Reset to filters", the accuracy line), Market insights, Compare companies.
+- **Job drawer:**
+  - The pay block, with honest-number labels; "Pay unclear" postings.
+  - The Juice waterfall: Monthly/Yearly and the household choice (Just me, Couple, Family).
+  - "Same role elsewhere", including Back.
+  - The Listing block, keywords, the lazy description and the Apply link (the right careers host).
+  - Copy link, next/prev, Esc and focus.
+- **Other features:**
+  - Save search and "N new"; Download CSV.
+  - Theme toggle (persists).
+  - URL hash round-trip, deep links and Back/Forward.
+  - Share pages /c/<slug>/.
+  - Keyboard shortcuts (/, t, j/k) not firing while typing.
+  - The data badge and its popover; the as-of dates; the methodology links (they open on-site).
+- **Errors:** no console errors anywhere.
+- **Beta only:**
+  - The page says clearly that it is beta.
+  - The big-tech boards load from the bundle only, with the badge saying Snapshot, not Live, and no live request.
+  - Paused companies are absent.
+  - A company with thousands of roles (Apple) stays responsive in every view: time the filter, sort and chart updates.
+  - Links back to the main site work.
+  - Big-tech pay ranges that span several levels are labelled honestly.
+
+Also run `npm test` and the full e2e suite, and report the results.
+
+For each bug, write: an ID (D-n, numbered after the highest ID in the newest sections of docs/process/lead.md (from "Beta round 3" on: fix wave 5, fix-density, google-grouping, the salary audit, perf-mobile-beta-2, fix6-fresh-data), docs/process/methodology-review-beta.md, docs/process/ux-review-beta.md, docs/process/viz-review-beta.md and the 2026-10-11 beta sections of docs/QA.md), a severity (Critical, High, Medium or Low), the viewport, exact repro steps, expected vs actual, a screenshot under docs/screenshots/qa-desktop-beta-3/, and the likely owning file and function. Keep it factual and say what works as well. Report back with the full bug list ordered by severity, one line each, and the suite results.
